From 5c029ad8a062bca00334c263eb178552b4937cbb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wk <58632380+wkai343@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:41:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: qcom: restore Cape GPU OPPs with GMU CX dependencies

Use the 13 SM8475 operating points from the fixed Liuqin OEM DT, including
GX voltage corners, independent CX floors and ACD droop controls. Remove
the inherited SM8450 OPP table before defining the replacement.

The GEN7 HFI GX performance entry has a CX corner index in its second
word, which was previously named acd and always disabled. Translate the
optional per-OPP CX levels using cx.lvl and preserve the disabled value
for every existing platform without the property. Reject partial or
unsupported tables and propagate power-table initialization failures.

Sources: MiCode kernel_devicetree 1c507816, Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource
eb49e100 (liuqin-t-oss), and OS2.0.6.0 vendor_boot DTB 02. The voltage
values are RPMh corners, not guessed microvolts. GMU 200/500 MHz OPPs
and the existing 12-level A730 bandwidth table already match the OEM.
---
